SUMMARY: Delta(n,m,gamma) ~ c(lambda,gamma) * n^( -1/2 )
        = [1/(12*lambda)] / sqrt(n),  independent of gamma,
as n->infinity at fixed lambda=m/sqrt(n). This is the leading
correction beyond the leading-order Laplace/Gaussian approximation
to the inner t-integral -- confirmed two independent ways above:
(B)/(C') exact leading-power algebra, and (C'') direct mpmath
dps=60 numerics with NO symbolic series machinery at all.
